{"id":"ce1461d3e7bc342b","group":"73","path":"73/73-thm-finite-residual-characterization.md","title":"Myhill–Nerode Theorem","display":"thm-myhill-nerode — Myhill–Nerode Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Automata Theory, Languages and Computation (Hopcroft, Ullman)","book_abbrev":"73","label":"73-thm-finite-residual-characterization","aliases":["73-thm-finite-residual-characterization","73-thm-myhill-nerode"],"display":"thm-myhill-nerode — Myhill–Nerode Theorem","depends_on":["[[73-df-language-residual-equivalence]]","[[73-df-finite-automaton-language-class]]","[[73-df-language-pumping-length]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Automata Theory, Languages and Computation (Hopcroft, Ullman)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"73"},{"key":"label","html":"73-thm-finite-residual-characterization"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>73-thm-finite-residual-characterization</span><span>73-thm-myhill-nerode</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-myhill-nerode — Myhill–Nerode Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"f41b3be50448ef3b\" href=\"?note=f41b3be50448ef3b\" title=\"73-df-language-residual-equivalence\">73-df-language-residual-equivalence</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"c284ffb568a496fd\" href=\"?note=c284ffb568a496fd\" title=\"73-df-finite-automaton-language-class\">73-df-finite-automaton-language-class</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"01b7b9d9615ddaa5\" href=\"?note=01b7b9d9615ddaa5\" title=\"73-df-language-pumping-length\">73-df-language-pumping-length</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma\">\\(\\Sigma\\)</span> (alphabet)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\\subseteq\\Sigma^*\">\\(L\\subseteq\\Sigma^*\\)</span> (language)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ind}(L)\">\\(\\operatorname{ind}(L)\\)</span> (Myhill–Nerode index, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"f41b3be50448ef3b\" href=\"?note=f41b3be50448ef3b\" title=\"73-df-language-residual-equivalence\">73-df-language-residual-equivalence</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p_{\\mathsf{reg}}(L)\">\\(p_{\\mathsf{reg}}(L)\\)</span> (minimum DFA state count for a regular language, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"01b7b9d9615ddaa5\" href=\"?note=01b7b9d9615ddaa5\" title=\"73-df-language-pumping-length\">73-df-language-pumping-length</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}myhill\\text{-}nerode}\\vdash\n\\forall L\\subseteq\\Sigma^*\\;\n\\bigl(L\\in\\mathsf{REG}_{\\Sigma}\n\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{ind}(L)&lt;\\aleph_0\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}myhill\\text{-}nerode}\\vdash\n\\forall L\\subseteq\\Sigma^*\\;\n\\bigl(L\\in\\mathsf{REG}_{\\Sigma}\n\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{ind}(L)&lt;\\aleph_0\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}myhill\\text{-}nerode}\\vdash\n\\forall L\\in\\mathsf{REG}_{\\Sigma}\\;\np_{\\mathsf{reg}}(L)=\\operatorname{ind}(L)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}myhill\\text{-}nerode}\\vdash\n\\forall L\\in\\mathsf{REG}_{\\Sigma}\\;\np_{\\mathsf{reg}}(L)=\\operatorname{ind}(L)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Every DFA state reached by a prefix determines one right quotient, so any recognizing DFA has at least <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ind}(L)\">\\(\\operatorname{ind}(L)\\)</span> reachable states.</li>\n<li>When the index is finite, the equivalence classes themselves form a DFA with transition <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"[x]_L\\xrightarrow{a}[xa]_L\">\\([x]_L\\xrightarrow{a}[xa]_L\\)</span>. This DFA is minimal.</li>\n<li>The former unconditional equation <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|Q_M|=\\operatorname{ind}(L)\">\\(|Q_M|=\\operatorname{ind}(L)\\)</span> was false for nonminimal DFAs and has been replaced by the minimum-state statement.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"73-df-language-residual-equivalence","status":"resolved","id":"f41b3be50448ef3b","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-language-residual-equivalence]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-finite-automaton-language-class","status":"resolved","id":"c284ffb568a496fd","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-finite-automaton-language-class]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-language-pumping-length","status":"resolved","id":"01b7b9d9615ddaa5","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-language-pumping-length]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-language-residual-equivalence","status":"resolved","id":"f41b3be50448ef3b","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{ind}(L)$ (Myhill–Nerode index, see [[73-df-language-residual-equivalence]])","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-language-pumping-length","status":"resolved","id":"01b7b9d9615ddaa5","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$p_{\\mathsf{reg}}(L)$ (minimum DFA state count for a regular language, see [[73-df-language-pumping-length]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\Sigma","display":false},{"tex":"L\\subseteq\\Sigma^*","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{ind}(L)","display":false},{"tex":"p_{\\mathsf{reg}}(L)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}myhill\\text{-}nerode}\\vdash\n\\forall L\\subseteq\\Sigma^*\\;\n\\bigl(L\\in\\mathsf{REG}_{\\Sigma}\n\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{ind}(L)<\\aleph_0\\bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}myhill\\text{-}nerode}\\vdash\n\\forall L\\in\\mathsf{REG}_{\\Sigma}\\;\np_{\\mathsf{reg}}(L)=\\operatorname{ind}(L)","display":true},{"tex":"\\operatorname{ind}(L)","display":false},{"tex":"[x]_L\\xrightarrow{a}[xa]_L","display":false},{"tex":"|Q_M|=\\operatorname{ind}(L)","display":false}],"bytes":1516,"backlinks":[{"id":"69901fc0f2bc2a70","anchor":"ref-5","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""}],"outgoing":["f41b3be50448ef3b","c284ffb568a496fd","01b7b9d9615ddaa5"]}